      "text": "Làm đềtrực tuyến tại: https://ielts-fighter.com/online-test.html\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        59.94099426269531,
        302.55078125,
        76.59700012207031
      ],
      "text": "Website tựhọc IELTS: https://ielts-fighter.com\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        84.99369812011719,
        518.8134765625,
        123.59259796142578
      ],
      "text": "money then who are we to charge for such a basic thing which we do not even\nown?\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        136.71470642089844,
        515.2467651367188,
        195.23361206054688
      ],
      "text": "We all have seen countries going to work claiming the ownership of the water\nresources and if one of them does win all the effort goes down to nothing\nwhen in the end they tax their own countrymen for it.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        208.2346954345703,
        521.8430786132812,
        286.6736145019531
      ],
      "text": "It is there that access to clean water is a basic human right. Therefore every\nhome should as water supply is free. It is the responsibility of the authorities to\nlook after the needs of the people as it is them who declared clean water as a\nbasic right.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        299.6110534667969,
        203.63038635253906,
        319.1124572753906
      ],
      "text": "[Examiner’s comment]\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        365.37103271484375,
        262.5813293457031,
        384.2682800292969
      ],
      "text": "Here is the examiner’s comment:\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        399.5146789550781,
        522.1749877929688,
        477.8336181640625
      ],
      "text": "This is a good response that provides relevant ideas. The writer expresses their\nposition, and agrees with the statement that access to clean water should be\nfree, although there is some repetition and some lack of clarity within the main\nideas expressed.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        490.95367431640625,
        518.4898071289062,
        628.9136352539062
      ],
      "text": "There are supporting arguments that include: whether any kind of water, or\nonly ‘clean water’ should be provided, whether people should be allowed to\n‘own’ the air we breathe and force people to pay for it, whether any person\nshould be the [sole protector] of the water supply and whether the aim is to\n[tax their own countrymen] for water. The conclusion states that governments\nhave declared that clean water is a basic right, and so they should look after\nthe needs of the people, and provide [every home] with a free water supply.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        630.0347290039062,
        517.4954833984375,
        708.3526000976562
      ],
      "text": "Ideas are generally logically organised, but there is a lack of progression\naround the sections that refer to the ownership of water on planet earth, with\nrepetition across three paragraphs (2, 3 and 4). However, generally, ideas are\narranged in order and we can follow the progression through the response.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        709.4747314453125,
        507.05487060546875,
        748.0736083984375
      ],
      "text": "Cohesive devices are used to some good effect, including referencing within\nsentences [while | us who | their own countrymen].\n"
    }
  ]
